  "body": "### Summary\nAs the operator, I want to decide whether Bookmarks, offline topics and AQ keep the system pull to refresh, now that the profile dropped its own (#1312, decision 2026-11-28), so that the lists agree with legacy and with each other.\n\n### Scope\nThe three lists that still carry `.refreshable`:\n- Bookmarks: `App/SwiftHFR/MPStorage/BookmarksView.swift:54`. Legacy has a pull: `HFRswift/Swift/BookmarksPlusView.swift:233` @ `87fe0d1c`.\n- AQ: `App/SwiftHFR/QualityAlerts/QualityAlertsView.swift:55`. Legacy has a pull: `HFRswift/Swift/AQPlusView.swift:442` @ `87fe0d1c`.\n- Offline topics: `App/SwiftHFR/Offline/OfflineTopicsView.swift:65`. No `refreshable` or `refreshControl` in legacy `HFRswift` at `87fe0d1c` (offline saving is disabled, GAP-180).\n\nLedger: `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md` « Other lists with the system `.refreshable` » (line 307) and the « Gap issues » line (309).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\nThe operator decides per list (keep or drop); then one PR applies it (test: no `UIRefreshControl` on the list for a drop, as #1445) and the GAP lines name the outcome.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
